<div className="os-modal-head"><div><span className="os-label">HOLLOW-7 / FIELD GUIDE</span><div className="os-modal-title">Build a place worth remembering.</div></div><button className="os-btn os-icon-btn" title="Close menu" @click={closeDialog}>×</button></div>
<div className="os-help-topics"><button className="os-btn os-tab" oson={String(helpTopic === "all")} @click={() => setHelpTopic("all")}>Everything</button><button className="os-btn os-tab" oson={String(helpTopic === "start")} @click={() => setHelpTopic("start")}>Getting started</button><button className="os-btn os-tab" oson={String(helpTopic === "people")} @click={() => setHelpTopic("people")}>People</button><button className="os-btn os-tab" oson={String(helpTopic === "frontier")} @click={() => setHelpTopic("frontier")}>Frontier</button><button className="os-btn os-tab" oson={String(helpTopic === "systems")} @click={() => setHelpTopic("systems")}>Systems</button></div>
<div className="os-help-grid">
#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
  <div className="os-stack"><div><div className="os-help-heading">Your first shift</div><span className="os-prose">Pause and plan. Place the 8 × 8 bunkhouse on clear ground northwest of the lifeboat. Add two sunroot plots. Gather trees to the west and ore to the east. Build a table so meals feel more like meals. Materials are reserved when you place blueprints.</span></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Power is a real network</div><span className="os-prose">A generator can run through the night, but needs fuel. Solar arrays work in daylight. Drag conduits between electrical footprints using the Build → Power category. The ϟ overlay shows cable paths. Separate circuits do not share electricity. Batteries store surplus energy. Critical equipment gets priority during a shortage.</span></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Food and industry</div><span className="os-prose">Fields must be sown before they grow. A full crop creates a harvest job, then a hauling trip. A field stove makes three meals from three raw food and one wood. The electric kitchen makes four meals from three raw food. Production targets are in Stock. Ore → smelter → metal → fabrication bench → components. Wood → biomass press → fuel.</span></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Keep the people alive</div><span className="os-prose">Colonists reserve food and beds automatically. A healthy colonist with Treat enabled tends injuries in the field; medicine improves recovery. Health below 22 means downed. Hunger, exhaustion, cold, and grief affect morale. A roof, a table, recreation, and supportive relationships help.</span></div></div>
#end
#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
  <div className="os-stack"><div><div className="os-help-heading">Map and time controls</div><div className="os-detail"><span>Pause / resume</span><b>Space</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Simulation speed</span><b>1 / 2 / 3 (or 4) = 1× / 2× / 4×</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Pan</span><b>Drag in Select mode / Pan button / arrows</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Zoom</span><b>+ / − or map buttons</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Return to camp</span><b>Home / ⌂</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Build / gather / survey</span><b>B / H / E</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Research / sunroot plot</span><b>R / F</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Grid / power overlay</span><b>G / P</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Draft selected colonist</span><b>D</b></div><div className="os-detail"><span>Field guide / close</span><b>? / Escape</b></div></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Defence without micromanaging life</div><span className="os-prose">Draft settlers to control their movement. Click ground to move, or a creature to target it. Weapon range and line of sight determine whether they can attack. Barricades provide adjacent cover. Colonists defend themselves from nearby threats automatically. Stand them down to return to work. A powered sentry covers eight tiles.</span></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Explore and remember</div><span className="os-prose">Survey orders reveal terrain as colonists travel. The first signal leads to Structure 17. Recover archives, then research the next interpretation to continue. Three recovered sites open three ending paths. The chronicle preserves discoveries, relationships, construction, and loss.</span></div><div><div className="os-help-heading">Save before updating</div><span className="os-prose">Three manual slots and three rotating autosaves live in this browser's app storage. Autosaves happen after 90 seconds of active foreground play. Use Export to text and keep a JSON copy before clearing site data or loading a new bundle. No offline simulation occurs while you are away.</span></div></div>
#end
</div>
<div className="os-modal-footer"><button className="os-btn os-primary" @click={closeDialog}>Back to the frontier</button></div>
#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
<div className="os-card"><div className="os-help-heading">Auto steward and camera</div><span className="os-prose">Use AUTO in the toolbar to gather known nearby wood, stone, ore and food up to reserve targets, and queue practical research. Colonists still follow work priorities, eat, rest, and obey drafted orders. You place buildings and decide Hollow encounters. Move the cursor to any map edge to pan, even while paused. The ↔ map button toggles edge scrolling.</span></div>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Weapons and frontier threats</div><span className="os-prose">Two pistols and two spears start south of camp. Select a settler, open Gear, choose a weapon, then resume so they can collect it. Draft to use it; select a defender to see their range circle. The circle shows distance, while walls and doors block line of sight. Spears reach 2 tiles, pistols 6, and carbines 9. Trade for weapons in Frontier; caravans leave purchases south of camp. Excavated archives can yield a carbine. Downed settlers drop their weapon. Unarmed automatic defenders try to retreat; manual drafted orders remain yours. Later predator packs include glass spitters with a 5-tile attack. Use walls for cover and carbines for distance. Sanctuary suppresses generated attacks.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "people")
<div className="os-help-heading">A life between jobs</div><span className="os-prose">Idle settlers use common rooms and gathering tables, visit memory stones, and take short walks on explored safe paths. Downtime improves recreation and nearby companions can build relationships. New eligible work interrupts these optional breaks; eating, sleep and defence still take precedence. Dangerous weather discourages outdoor wandering. Unarmed idle settlers may collect an available weapon; dropping one manually opts that settler out until you request another. Build essentials remains a separate choice in Work.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">The signal chapters</div><span className="os-prose">The Settlement panel follows six chapters from touchdown to the choice beneath the stone. Each lists three goals drawn from the live colony: shelter and a hot meal, a harvest and a light, the first signal, the buried ward, the listening engine, and the ending you power. Goal shortcuts open the matching tool, panel or ruin. Finishing a chapter opens a narrated beat with a small consequence, and you can re-read the last beat at any time. Established colonies and older saves start at the chapter they have already earned. Chapters run under every incident setting, including Off.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Predators without an appointment</div><span className="os-prose">From Sol 4 on Frontier, packs can approach without a story prompt, most often at night. A warning enters the chronicle about an hour before they arrive, and the Settlement panel shows an incoming alert. Packs grow slowly with the Sol count and population; Severe permits larger ones, Relaxed spaces them out, and Sanctuary, Gentle or Off prevent them. Waves never stack on an active attack and hold off while half the colony is hurt. Mining ore or reaching Sol 8 can draw a burrow maw: slow, armoured and hard-biting, best fought at range or from behind barricades. Fallen creatures fade after half a Sol and herbivores wander back from the map edge, so hunting remains possible.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Frontier voices</div><span className="os-prose">Beyond the chapters, one-off encounters branch off what you have done: an escape pod on the northern slope, Sol's last seed packet, the Pilgrim on the ridge, Ashwalker nomads who want your metal, the Choir singing on the maintenance band once a mast is powered, the date on Jin's inspection tag, and a dream everyone shares. Most wait their turn on the incident timer; the Hollow ones arrive on their day even with incidents Off. Frontier shows your standing with the Meridian Compact, Helix Recovery and the Choir, and a perimeter note that hints at what the frontier has noticed. Turning the Ashwalkers away, or growing rich, invites raiders: they fight anyone within reach, take metal, meals, components and medicine from the racks or lifeboat, and run for the map edge. Bring them down to recover the goods. Predators that cannot reach anyone chew through walls, doors and barricades; builders repair the damage and defenders end it.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "systems")
<div className="os-help-heading">Sound that stays on</div><span className="os-prose">Sound, music, effects, volume and narration choices are remembered on this device. After a reload the menu shows "Sound ready · tap to play" until your first click or key press, because browsers do not allow audio before a gesture; the theme then resumes on its own.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "systems")
<div className="os-help-heading">Background play</div><span className="os-prose">By default the colony keeps running when the window loses focus. Browsers slow hidden tabs to about one update a second, so the game recovers up to a minute of simulation per update; at 1× a hidden tab keeps real-time pace, at 4× it runs slower than the foreground would. Turn Background play off in the pause menu to pause whenever the window loses focus, as earlier versions did. The setting is remembered on this device.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Striking back</div><span className="os-prose">Raiders who escape with goods make camp at the map edge for three Sols. Frontier and the map show the camp and what it holds. Send a strike party: an explorer walks to the camp, the Ashwalkers turn to fight, and when the last defender falls the stolen goods are left among the tents for haulers to bring home. Arm the explorer and draft the rest before they arrive. Later in the story, Helix will bid for your Echo cores, the Choir will ask you not to silence the engine, the Compact may offer a charter that doubles caravan visits, and each founder gets a moment of their own. Endings read differently depending on who you kept faith with. The Chronicle now opens with the colony's record.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "systems")
<div className="os-help-heading">A research queue</div><span className="os-prose">Research cards now have Queue next. Queue up to eight projects, including ones whose prerequisites are still being researched; when the station clears, the first queued project that is available begins on its own and the chronicle notes it. The active project card shows how many are waiting; press the queue button again to remove one.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "systems")
<div className="os-help-heading">Saving without the clipboard</div><span className="os-prose">Refreshing or closing the page autosaves the colony and reopens it on your next visit. Save → Download save file hands your browser a .json file for its download folder; Open a save file… restores from one you choose; pasted text still works. Exporting the chronicle downloads a text file too.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Landing sites and mossback pens</div><span className="os-prose">Expedition settings now offer three landing sites. Lantern Hills is the original valley. Rust Flats is ore-rich and timber-poor, with hot days and glass on the wind; you land with extra ore and metal but less wood. Verdant Basin is thick with timber and berries, wet and foggy, and short on ore. The site colours the map and shifts the climate and weather. Research Mossback husbandry, build a grazing pen (Food, 18 wood), then select a mossback and choose Tame: a farmer walks out with six raw food, and the animal joins the pen, grazes for 6 raw food a Sol, and never turns hostile. A pen holds three; cull one from the pen's card for 18 raw food.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "people")
<div className="os-help-heading">A bunkhouse from the steward, and a chronicle to keep</div><span className="os-prose">With Build essentials on, the steward now raises the first eight-by-eight bunkhouse itself once the farms are planned, from Sol 2, when it can spare 167 wood and 12 metal and find clear ground near camp. Until then it places loose cots as before. The Chronicle panel can export the whole record and every entry as plain text into the save box, ready to copy and keep.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "people")
<div className="os-help-heading">The second generation</div><span className="os-prose">From Sol 15, partners in a stable colony (good mood and health, three Sols of food, a cot for everyone) may have a child. You choose the name from two the parents picked. A young child does not work; from eight Sols they help with hauling, farming and cooking at a child's pace and learn fastest beside a parent. Twenty Sols later they come of age: follow a parent's trade for a strong start in it, or find their own way. Predators with nobody in reach now go for sentry turrets and power equipment, and glass spitters spit at them from range; repairs and defenders answer as usual. Mods can now tell their own stories: see the modding guide.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Hunting and the seasons</div><span className="os-prose">Select a mossback or needlehare and choose Designate for hunting. An armed settler with Explore enabled tracks it, brings it down, and haulers fetch the meat (18 raw food from a mossback, 4 from a needlehare). A wounded mossback fights back, so send a pistol or a carbine. With Auto on, the steward marks a nearby animal when food runs short. Every twelve Sols the season turns and the chronicle says what to expect: Longlight is warm and bright, Emberfall cools, and Deepcold freezes outdoor sunroot for twelve Sols, so plan heaters, fuel, Hollowcap beds or hydroponics before it arrives. At a funeral you now choose who speaks; the chronicle records what they said.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "people")
<div className="os-help-heading">Holding the line</div><span className="os-prose">Automatic defenders who carry a weapon now close the distance to a hostile they cannot reach or see, so spear carriers no longer stand still while a spitter shoots them; drafted settlers under your own orders still hold. Predators go for whoever is standing and only turn on the downed when nobody else is near. Wounds clot on their own within a minute or two (faster asleep), so an untreated settler stabilises instead of bleeding out; treatment still heals. Waves on Normal are spaced further apart, grow more slowly, and pause for a Sol after a death or while a funeral is on. Raiders take less per visit.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
<div className="os-help-heading">Stories as captions</div><span className="os-prose">Encounters and chapter beats now appear as a caption strip over the map, with narration if sound is on, while the colony keeps running and the map stays usable. Answer from the strip, or press ⤢ to open the full dialog. A thin timer shows how long you have; if nobody answers, the story resolves to the safe default named under the choices and the chronicle notes it. The timer pauses with the game. The pause menu can switch back to dialogs that wait.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "people")
<div className="os-help-heading">Burials and funerals</div><span className="os-prose">When a settler dies their body stays where they fell and the Settlement panel warns you. Build a grave (Build → People, 4 stone). A hauler carries the fallen to it, and a funeral begins: everyone who is not drafted, hungry or exhausted walks to the graveside and pays respects for a while. Attending softens grief, more so for close friends, and the chronicle records who stood there. A grave holds one settler and shows who rests in it when selected.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "frontier")
<div className="os-help-heading">Long nights</div><span className="os-prose">Lanternwings come out over the lake on clear nights from Sol 2: small glowing fliers that fade at dawn and settle anyone who sees them. Settlers now learn from real work; each skill rises slowly with the jobs they actually do, faster for disciplined people, and the chronicle notes every full point. The world's first moments get their own stories: the first Glass Wind, the first Echo Rain, the first loss and the first turn of the season, plus Sol's table once sixty meals have been cooked. Two Sols after any ending, an epilogue arrives.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
<div className="os-help-heading">Setting out alone</div><span className="os-prose">Select a healthy settler and choose Set out alone. They take up to eight meals and leave the colony's active ground; the view follows them, and right-clicking sends them on. The country is generated from the seed as they reach it and is the same whenever anyone comes back to it. Return to colony brings them home; they rest under the sky when tired and eat from their pack when hungry, and starve if it runs out.</span>
<div className="os-help-heading">Cancelling plans</div><span className="os-prose">Choose Dismantle, then drag a box (mouse or one finger) to cancel every unbuilt blueprint and gathering designation inside it with a full refund. A single click still dismantles a built structure for half its materials. The Build panel's Cancel all button clears every blueprint in the colony at once. Each settler's card now shows their temperament: curiosity speeds research, empathy improves treatment and calms arguments, and nerve decides how much worry they can carry before needing a moment.</span>
#end

#if (helpTopic === "all" || helpTopic === "start")
<div className="os-help-heading">Mouse and touch orders</div><span className="os-prose">Right-click cancels an active tool. With Select active and a healthy settler selected, right-click explored ground to draft and move them, or a creature to target it. Stand down from their panel to resume work. On a phone, tap to inspect, drag with one finger to pan, and pinch with two fingers to zoom. Choose a building or designation, tap the tile, then press Apply here. Dragging always pans on touch. Select a settler and press Draft before tapping a move or attack destination. Close panel keeps your selection; Cancel / clear removes it. Scroll the roster and resource strip sideways on small screens. Panels and menus scroll vertically.</span>
#end
